// Hunt: PowerShell -EncodedCommand extraction and decode
// Table: DeviceCustomScriptEvents
// Purpose: Pull the base64 payload out of a -EncodedCommand invocation on the
//          initiating process command line and decode it for review. PowerShell
//          encodes -EncodedCommand as UTF-16LE, so the decoded text will show
//          interleaved null bytes when rendered as plain UTF-8. This is
//          expected and not a query defect. For clean text, post process the
//          EncodedPortion with base64_decode_toarray plus a UTF-16 aware
//          string conversion outside of KQL, or eyeball the decoded text with
//          the nulls stripped.
// Extracts and decodes the base64 payload from a PowerShell
// -EncodedCommand flag. Interleaved nulls in the decoded text are expected.
DeviceCustomScriptEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(7d)
| where InitiatingProcessCommandLine contains '-EncodedCommand'
| extend EncodedPortion = extract(@'(?i)encodedcommand\s+([A-Za-z0-9+/=]{20,})', 1, InitiatingProcessCommandLine)
| where isnotempty(EncodedPortion)
| extend DecodedAttempt = base64_decode_tostring(EncodedPortion)
| project Timestamp, DeviceName, InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessAccountName, EncodedPortion, DecodedAttempt, RuleName
| order by Timestamp desc
| take 10000
